			"content": "<h3>\n<a></a>Top Links</h3>\n<ul><li>\n<a href=\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/visualstudio/removing-out-of-support-components-from-your-visual-studio-installations/\">Removing out-of-support components from your Visual Studio installations</a> (Christine Ruana)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://platform.uno/blog/replicating-food-delivery-app-ui-with-uno-platform/\">Replicating Food Delivery App UI with Uno Platform</a> (Uno Platform Team)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://bea.stollnitz.com/blog/configure-dev-machine/\">Configuring your Windows development machine for data science</a> (Bea Stollnitz)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://www.arm.com/blogs/blueprint/windows-on-arm-laptop-momentum?utm_source=linkedin&amp;utm_medium=social&amp;utm_content=blog&amp;utm_campaign=na_na_na_na_na\">Windows on Arm: Accelerating momentum for the future of laptop computing</a> (David Whaley)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://code.visualstudio.com/blogs/2022/11/28/vscode-sandbox\">VS Code Sandboxing</a> (Benjamin Pasero)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3>\n<a></a>Web &amp; Cloud Development</h3>\n<ul><li>\n<a href=\"https://www.bennadel.com/blog/4360-using-picture-and-source-tags-to-prevent-loading-hero-image-on-mobile-devices.htm\">Using Picture And Source Tags To Prevent Loading Hero Image On Mobile Devices</a> (Ben Nadel)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://daverupert.com/2022/11/html5-video-capture-frame-still/\">How to capture single frame from an HTML video</a> (Dave Rupert)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://code.tutsplus.com/tutorials/learn-computer-science-with-javascript-part-4-functions--cms-29326\">Learn to Code With JavaScript: Part 4, Functions</a> (Alberta Williams)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://dev.to/officialbidisha/creating-async-task-runner-with-concurrency-in-javascript-49j9\">Creating Async Task Runner with Concurrency in JavaScript</a> (Bidisha Das)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://www.textcontrol.com/blog/2022/11/29/deploying-document-viewer-to-linux/\">ASP.NET Core: Deploying the TX Text Control Document Viewer to Azure App Services</a> (Bjoern Meyer)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://www.sitepoint.com/make-javascript-functional/?utm_source=rss\">5 Ways to Make Your JavaScript More Functional</a> (Darren Jones &amp; Olivia Gibson)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://thenewstack.io/confidential-compute-on-azure-with-kubernetes/\">Confidential Compute on Azure with Kubernetes</a> (Mary Branscombe)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/windows-dev-appconsult/build-a-web-app-to-manage-a-custom-provider-in-viva-learning/ba-p/3686343\">Build a web app to manage a custom provider in Viva Learning with Blazor</a> (Matteo Pagani)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://www.learmoreseekmore.com/2022/11/dotnet7-webapi-azure-blob-storage-file-management-example.html\">.NET 7 | Web API | Azure Blob Storage | File Management | Example</a> (Naveen Bommidi)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://www.infragistics.com/community/blogs/b/infragistics/posts/top-5-angular-data-grid-features\">The Top 5 Angular Data Grid Features You Never Knew You Needed</a> (Zdravko Kolev)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://ifelse.io/2022/11/29/some-helpful-free-apis-i-run-with-fly.io/\">Some Helpful, Free APIs I Run with Fly.io</a> (Mark Thomas)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://www.syncfusion.com/blogs/post/8-common-http-error-codes-and-their-possible-fixes.aspx?utm_source=alvinashcraft&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=alvinashcraft_blog_edmnov22\">8 Common HTTP Error Codes and Their Possible Fixes</a> (Aarthi Manoharan)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"http://healthcaresecprivacy.blogspot.com/2022/11/privacy-consent-on-fhir-looking-for.html\">Privacy Consent on FHIR – looking for initial feedback</a> (John Moehrke)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v19.2.0\">Node v19.2.0 (Current)</a> (Ruy Adorno)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3>\n<a></a>WinUI, .NET MAUI &amp; XAML</h3>\n<ul><li>\n<a href=\"https://www.syncfusion.com/blogs/post/achieve-outlook-like-swiping-using-net-maui-listview.aspx?utm_source=alvinashcraft&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=alvinashcraft_blog_edmnov22\">Achieve Outlook-Like Swiping Using .NET MAUI ListView</a> (Jayaleshwari N.)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://www.telerik.com/blogs/recap-state-dotnet-maui-net-conf-2022\">Recap: State of .NET MAUI—.NET Conf 2022</a> (Leomaris Reyes)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3>\n<a></a>Visual Studio &amp; .NET</h3>\n<ul><li>\n<a href=\"https://www.grapecity.com/blogs/use-a-c-sharp-net-text-parser-to-extract-data-and-add-it-to-desktop-apps\">Use a C# .NET Text Parser to Extract Data and Add it to Desktop Apps</a> (Kartik Sagar)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://anthonygiretti.com/2022/11/29/introducing-c11-list-pattern/\">Introducing C#11: List Pattern</a> (Anthony Giretti)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://www.textcontrol.com/blog/2022/11/29/adding-digital-signatures-to-pdf-documents-in-csharp/\">Adding Digital Signatures to PDF Documents in C#</a> (Bjoern Meyer)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://code-maze.com/csharp-difference-between-isnull-and-equality-operators/\">Difference Between Is and Equality Operators in C# – “is null” vs “== null”</a> (Code Maze)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://developers.redhat.com/articles/2022/11/30/c-11-raw-strings-required-members-and-auto-default-structs\">C# 11: Raw strings, required members, and auto-default structs</a> (Tom Deseyn)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"http://i-programmer.info/news/105-artificial-intelligence/15903-microsoft-mlnet-2-adds-text-classification-api.html\">Microsoft ML.NET 2 Adds Text Classification API</a> (Kay Ewbank)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/oldnewthing/20221129-00/?p=107478\">Dubious security vulnerability: Reading the files in the WindowsApps folder</a> (Raymond Chen)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/cppblog/msvc-openmp-update/\">MSVC OpenMP Update</a> (Tanveer Gani)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3>\n<a></a>Design, Methodology &amp; Testing</h3>\n<ul><li>\n<a href=\"https://ayende.com/blog/198593-A/fundamental-knowledge?Key=4c32a950-455e-418e-bae4-5110b84357e0\">Fundamental knowledge</a> (Oren Eini)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://timdeschryver.dev/blog/intercepting-http-requests-with-playwright\">Intercepting HTTP Requests with Playwright</a> (Tim Deschryver)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/device-management-in-microsoft/how-the-management-team-at-ms-integrates-with-engineering/ba-p/3685630\">How the management team at MS integrates with engineering</a> (James Lieurance)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://joemayo.medium.com/a-beginners-overview-of-software-development-229d4861dd76?source=rss-c868a333b1d6------2\">A Beginner’s Overview of Software Development</a> (Joe Mayo)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://dev.to/devsatasurion/make-prs-the-best-part-of-programming-1l95\">Make PRs the BEST PART of Programming</a> (Kaeden Wile)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3>\n<a></a>Mobile, IoT &amp; Game Development</h3>\n<ul><li>\n<a href=\"https://code.tutsplus.com/tutorials/android-sdk-common-android-components--mobile-20873\">Android SDK: Common Android Components</a> (Sue Smith)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://blog.mozilla.org/en/mozilla/mozilla-hubs-3d-vr-platform/\">3 ways to use Mozilla Hubs, a VR platform that’s accessible and private by design</a> (Kristina Bravo)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3>\n<a></a>Screencasts &amp; Videos</h3>\n<ul><li>\n<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2vzTqIFVX78\">Start your metadata driven adventure in Azure Data Factory | Data Exposed: MVP Edition</a> (Anna Hoffman)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rFJHY7YK6V4\">Effective Alerts with Snackbar &amp; Toast with .NET MAUI</a> (Gerald Versluis)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EXmSmv5ifkk\">Migrating &amp; Upgrading Xamarin.Forms to .NET MAUI</a> (James Montemagno)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JiEQffv8HvQ\">Getting started with .NET MAUI with Jack Pettit | .NET MAUI Hack day 2022</a> <em>and</em> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KV7I1BDFSoQ\">Building a simple mail client with .NET MAUI with Brady Stroud | .NET MAUI Hack day 2022</a> (SSW TV)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hVUQNmLC9hc\">You should benchmark your .NET apps</a> (Daniel Hindrikes)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CHzlj_r5CNU\">FreeCodeSession – Episode 417</a> (Jason Bock)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_YL8wvON0-I\">Armchair Architects: So, you want to build a platform … (Part 2)</a> (David Blank-Edelman, Uli Homann &amp; Eric Charran)</li>\n</ul><p></p>\n<h3>\n<a></a>Podcasts</h3>\n<ul><li>\n<a href=\"https://www.codenewbie.org/podcast/demonstrating-curiosity-kindly-with-matt-newkirk\">CodeNewbie S22:E3 – Demonstrating curiosity kindly with Matt Newkirk</a> (CodeNewbie Team)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://www.bennadel.com/blog/4361-working-code-podcast-episode-103-birdsite-go-boom.htm\">Working Code Podcast – Episode 103: Birdsite Go Boom</a> (Ben Nadel)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://changelog.com/practicalai/202\">Practical AI Podcast – Copilot lawsuits &amp; Galactica “science”</a> (Chris Benson &amp; Daniel Whitenack)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://ryanripley.com/yds-how-do-you-handle-a-defensive-scrum-team-in-a-retro/\">Your Daily Scrum: How Do You Handle a Defensive Scrum Team in a Retro?</a> (Ryan Ripley)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/shoptalkshow-ep-543/\">Shop Talk Show #593: Zach Leatherman on Eleventy, Mastodon, Twitter, and is-land</a> (Zach Leatherman)</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://anchor.fm/a-developer-experience/episodes/In-betweener-Fluidity-and-context-in-our-systems-e1retjh?utm_source=web&amp;utm_campaign=web-share&amp;utm_medium=sharing&amp;_branch_referrer=H4sIAAAAAAAAA8soKSkottLXLy7IL8lMq0zMS87IL9ItT03SSywo0MvJzMvWT9UvMvBNSk4rNc4pSwIA4xXCZDAAAAA%3D&amp;%24web_only=true&amp;_branch_match_id=1126304060361859930\">A Developer Experience Podcast – In-betweener: Fluidity and context in our systems</a> (Steven Hicks)</li>\n<li